≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 39.7%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 11.38"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":110.33,"default_fair_val":110.33,"premium_pct":73.4,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":24,"pe_forward":21.1,"pb_trailing":15.7,"pb_forward":14.1,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":6.6,"fcf_to_ev":4.13,"fcf_to_mcap":3.8,"liab_to_assets":39.7,"cash_to_assets":91.1,"current_ratio":11.38,"roe":-67.8,"roa":-40.9,"moat":{"ticker":"RVMD","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Revolution Medicines 在生物技術領域的品牌定價權極為有限。其產品尚處於臨床開發階段，尚未產生營收，更遑論建立品牌忠誠度或享有定價權。與成熟藥企不同，其價值依賴於未來臨床試驗的成功與監管批准，而非現有品牌聲譽。目前來看，品牌定價權幾乎不存在，屬於極弱壁壘。","comment_en":"Revolution Medicines has extremely limited brand pricing power in the biotechnology sector. Its products are still in clinical development and have not generated revenue, let alone established brand loyalty or pricing power. Unlike established pharmaceutical companies, its value depends on future clinical trial success and regulatory approval, not existing brand reputation. Currently, brand pricing power is virtually non-existent, representing a very weak barrier."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":9,"comment_zh":"Revolution Medicines 的核心競爭力來自其專利保護的創新療法。其專利組合涵蓋了獨特的分子和作用機制，為其研發的腫瘤藥物提供了強大的法律保護。這構成了顯著的進入壁壘，因為競爭對手難以繞過這些專利。監管批准過程本身也是一道高牆，需要巨額投入和時間，進一步鞏固了其潛在的市場地位。這是其最堅實的護城河。","comment_en":"Revolution Medicines' core competitive strength stems from its patent-protected innovative therapies. Its patent portfolio covers unique molecules and mechanisms of action, providing robust legal protection for its developed oncology drugs. This constitutes a significant entry barrier, as competitors find it difficult to circumvent these patents. The regulatory approval process itself is also a high wall, requiring substantial investment and time, further solidifying its potential market position. This is its most solid moat."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"對於 Revolution Medicines 而言，轉換成本壁壘目前幾乎不存在。由於其產品尚未商業化，醫生和患者尚未對特定療法產生依賴。一旦產品獲批上市，雖然臨床上可能存在一定的治療慣性，但與成熟藥物相比，其轉換成本相對較低。競爭對手若能提供更優的療效或更低的成本，患者轉換的可能性較高。","comment_en":"For Revolution Medicines, switching cost barriers are currently almost non-existent. As its products are not yet commercialized, physicians and patients have not developed dependence on specific therapies. Once products are approved and launched, while there might be some treatment inertia clinically, the switching costs are relatively low compared to established drugs. If competitors can offer superior efficacy or lower costs, the likelihood of patient switching is higher."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Revolution Medicines 的業務模式不涉及網絡效應。其藥物的價值和市場接受度主要取決於臨床療效、安全性以及專利保護，而非用戶數量或互動。與社交媒體或市場平台不同，其產品的邊際效益不會隨著用戶增加而提升。因此，網絡效應在此幾乎為零，無法構成護城河。","comment_en":"Revolution Medicines' business model does not involve network effects. The value and market acceptance of its drugs depend primarily on clinical efficacy, safety, and patent protection, not on user numbers or interactions. Unlike social media or marketplace platforms, the marginal benefit of its products does not increase with more users. Therefore, network effects are virtually zero here and cannot form a moat."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Revolution Medicines 目前尚未形成顯著的規模成本優勢。作為一家處於臨床階段的生物技術公司，其生產規模相對較小，難以與大型製藥公司在採購、生產效率上競爭。雖然未來產品成功上市後，規模效應可能有所體現，但短期內，這並非其核心競爭力或護城河。","comment_en":"Revolution Medicines has not yet established a significant cost advantage through scale. As a biotechnology company in the clinical stage, its production scale is relatively small, making it difficult to compete with large pharmaceutical companies in procurement and production efficiency. While economies of scale may become apparent after successful product launches in the future, this is not its core competency or moat in the short term."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Revolution Medicines 的業務高度依賴於其研發能力和知識產權，而非特定的地理位置或獨特資產。其臨床試驗可能在全球範圍內進行，但並無特定地理區域的壟斷性優勢。其核心價值在於科學創新，而非土地、礦產或特定地區的市場准入壁壘。因此，獨特地理資產壁壘幾乎為零。","comment_en":"Revolution Medicines' business relies heavily on its R&D capabilities and intellectual property, rather than specific geographic locations or unique assets. Its clinical trials may be conducted globally, but there is no monopolistic advantage in any particular geographic region. Its core value lies in scientific innovation, not in land, minerals, or market access barriers in specific areas. Therefore, the barrier from unique geographic assets is almost zero."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Revolution Medicines 在其研發和臨床試驗流程中展現了一定的營運效率，這在其快速推進多項臨床項目中有所體現。然而，與成熟的製藥巨頭相比，其營運效率仍有提升空間，尤其是在大規模商業化生產和銷售方面。目前的分數反映了其在研發階段的效率，但尚未達到能構成強大護城河的水平。","comment_en":"Revolution Medicines demonstrates a certain level of operational efficiency in its R&D and clinical trial processes, as evidenced by its rapid advancement of multiple clinical programs. However, compared to mature pharmaceutical giants, there is still room for improvement in its operational efficiency, especially in large-scale commercial production and sales. The current score reflects its efficiency during the R&D phase but has not yet reached a level that constitutes a strong moat."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Revolution Medicines 的資本配置策略似乎專注於將資金投入到最有前景的研發項目，以最大化未來潛在回報。公司擁有充足的現金儲備，並能有效管理其債務水平，顯示出一定的財務紀律。然而，作為一家仍在虧損的生物技術公司，其資本配置的長期有效性仍有待市場驗證。目前來看，其對研發的聚焦是合理的，但尚未達到頂尖水平。","comment_en":"Revolution Medicines' capital allocation strategy appears focused on investing funds into the most promising R&D projects to maximize future potential returns. The company possesses ample cash reserves and effectively manages its debt levels, indicating some financial discipline. However, as a biotechnology company still incurring losses, the long-term effectiveness of its capital allocation remains to be validated by the market. Currently, its focus on R&D is reasonable but has not yet reached the highest level."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Revolution Medicines 目前沒有客戶留存的問題，因為其產品尚未上市銷售。一旦產品獲批，客戶（患者）的留存將取決於療效、安全性、副作用以及與其他治療方案的比較。雖然成功的藥物能帶來一定的患者忠誠度，但與消費品或服務業的客戶留存概念不同，其壁壘相對較弱，且易受新藥的挑戰。","comment_en":"Revolution Medicines currently has no customer retention issues as its products are not yet on the market. Once products are approved, customer (patient) retention will depend on efficacy, safety, side effects, and comparison with other treatment options. While successful drugs can foster some patient loyalty, it differs from the concept of customer retention in consumer goods or service industries; the barrier is relatively weak and susceptible to challenges from new drugs."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Revolution Medicines 的業務模式具有潛在的長期可持續性，主要依賴於其持續的科學創新和專利保護。如果其研發的藥物能夠成功上市並獲得市場認可，其專利將在相當長的時間內提供市場獨佔性。然而，生物技術行業的快速發展和潛在的顛覆性技術是其面臨的主要風險。其護城河的持久性高度依賴於研發的持續成功。","comment_en":"Revolution Medicines' business model has potential long-term sustainability, primarily relying on its continuous scientific innovation and patent protection. If its developed drugs are successfully launched and gain market acceptance, its patents will provide market exclusivity for a considerable period. However, the rapid advancements and potential disruptive technologies in the biotechnology industry pose significant risks. The durability of its moat is highly dependent on sustained R&D success."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Revolution Medicines 的護城河主要建立在其專利保護和持續的研發創新之上，這構成了其最強的壁壘（M2、M10）。然而，公司目前仍處於臨床開發階段，尚未產生營收，這意味著品牌定價權（M1）、轉換成本（M3）、網絡效應（M4）、規模成本（M5）、地理優勢（M6）和客戶留存（M9）等傳統護城河維度幾乎為零。其營運效率（M7）和資本配置（M8）尚可，但有待市場驗證。總體而言，其護城河尚在構建中，高度依賴未來藥物的成功，屬於潛在的特許經營模式，但風險較高。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Revolution Medicines' moat is primarily built upon its patent protection and continuous R&D innovation, forming its strongest barriers (M2, M10). However, the company is still in the clinical development stage and has not yet generated revenue, meaning traditional moat dimensions such as brand pricing power (M1), switching costs (M3), network effects (M4), cost advantage of scale (M5), unique geography assets (M6), and customer retention (M9) are virtually non-existent. Its operational efficiency (M7) and capital allocation (M8) are acceptable but await market validation. Overall, its moat is still under construction, highly dependent on the success of future drugs, representing a potential franchise model but with high risk.","evidenceHash":"2a385f3c63142fc483bf08b1aef6bd9d582a148795d88a4cf7487f742e6fbee0","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T02:49:34.549Z","evidenceHash":"94828a9a7d58980c81791b81441d37fc78ed40d59fc3f4569730426d6406c413"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2023-12-31","period":"FY 2023","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T02:49:34.549Z","evidenceHash":"94828a9a7d58980c81791b81441d37fc78ed40d59fc3f4569730426d6406c413"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/RVMD.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/RVMD.png","website":"https://www.revmed.com","ceo":"Mark A. Goldsmith","full_time_employees":"883","description":"Revolution Medicines, Inc. is a precision oncology firm operating in the clinical development stage, dedicated to creating innovative treatments that target novel pathways crucial for RAS-driven cancers. Its pipeline includes several promising drug candidates: RMC-4630, an SHP2 inhibitor, is currently undergoing Phase 1/2 clinical trials for various solid tumors, such as gynecological and colorectal cancers. The company's portfolio also features RMC-5845, a selective inhibitor designed to target SOS1, a protein responsible for activating RAS within cells, and RMC-5552, a highly selective inhibitor for hyperactive mTORC1 signaling found in cancerous cells. Further expanding its therapeutic arsenal, Revolution Medicines is advancing RMC-6291, which selectively inhibits mutated forms of KRASG12C(ON) and NRASG12C(ON). Another promising compound, RMC-6236, specifically targets and inhibits a range of active RAS(ON) variants. Its research efforts also encompass other active RAS inhibitors aimed at KRASG13C(ON) and KRASG12D(ON) mutations. Revolution Medicines has established a collaborative partnership with Sanofi to research and develop SHP2 inhibitors, a collaboration that includes the development of RMC-4630. Established in 2014, Revolution Medicines, Inc. operates from its corporate headquarters situated in Redwood City, California.","description_en":"Revolution Medicines, Inc. is a precision oncology firm operating in the clinical development stage, dedicated to creating innovative treatments that target novel pathways crucial for RAS-driven cancers. Its pipeline includes several promising drug candidates: RMC-4630, an SHP2 inhibitor, is currently undergoing Phase 1/2 clinical trials for various solid tumors, such as gynecological and colorectal cancers. The company's portfolio also features RMC-5845, a selective inhibitor designed to target SOS1, a protein responsible for activating RAS within cells, and RMC-5552, a highly selective inhibitor for hyperactive mTORC1 signaling found in cancerous cells. Further expanding its therapeutic arsenal, Revolution Medicines is advancing RMC-6291, which selectively inhibits mutated forms of KRASG12C(ON) and NRASG12C(ON). Another promising compound, RMC-6236, specifically targets and inhibits a range of active RAS(ON) variants. Its research efforts also encompass other active RAS inhibitors aimed at KRASG13C(ON) and KRASG12D(ON) mutations. Revolution Medicines has established a collaborative partnership with Sanofi to research and develop SHP2 inhibitors, a collaboration that includes the development of RMC-4630. Established in 2014, Revolution Medicines, Inc. operates from its corporate headquarters situated in Redwood City, California.","description_zh":"Revolution Medicines, Inc.（美股代碼：RVMD）為 Healthcare 領域之重要企業，專注於 Biotechnology 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"700 Saginaw Drive","city":"Redwood City","state":"CA","zip":"94063","country":"US","phone":"650 481 6801","full_address":"700 Saginaw Drive, Redwood City, CA 94063, US","range_52w":"56.66-224.31","year_high":224.31,"year_low":56.66,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":56.66,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-28","name":"Mancini Anthony","title":"officer: See Remarks","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":2310,"price":33.62,"total_val":0.08},{"date":"2026-10-28","name":"Mancini Anthony","title":"officer: See Remarks","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":2310,"price":33.62,"total_val":0.08},{"date":"2026-10-28","name":"Mancini Anthony","title":"officer: See Remarks","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":2310,"price":186.99,"total_val":0.43},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Sandler Alan B.","title":"officer: Chief Development Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":6000,"price":58.84,"total_val":0.35},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Sandler Alan B.","title":"officer: Chief Development Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":6000,"price":58.84,"total_val":0.35},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Sandler Alan B.","title":"officer: Chief Development Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":2200,"price":200.82,"total_val":0